        "module": "philosophers-thinkers",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "philosophers-thinkers",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Philosophers and Thinkers - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nPHILOSOPHY\n├── METAPHYSICS ─── what exists? (ontology, substance, causation, time)\n├── EPISTEMOLOGY ── how do we know? (justification, skepticism, truth)\n├── LOGIC ──────── what follows from what? (validity, inference, formal systems)\n├── ETHICS ─────── what should we do? (normative theory, meta-ethics)\n├── POLITICAL ───── how should societies be organized?\n├── PHILOSOPHY OF MIND ── what is consciousness? (qualia, intentionality)\n├── PHILOSOPHY OF LANGUAGE ── how does language mean? (reference, truth)\n└── PHILOSOPHY OF SCIENCE ── what makes knowledge scientific?\n```"
    },
    {
