        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Philosophers and Thinkers - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| CS Concept | Philosophical Origin |\n|------------|---------------------|\n| Formal logic / proof systems | Frege's Begriffsschrift (1879) — first predicate logic |\n| Type theory | Russell's ramified theory of types (response to his own paradox) |\n| The halting problem / undecidability | Hilbert's Entscheidungsproblem — the question Church/Turing answered |\n| Lambda calculus | Church — grew directly from philosophical logic tradition |\n| Modal logic / possible worlds | Kripke — now standard in program verification, epistemic logic |\n| Formal semantics | Frege's sense/reference → Tarski's truth theory → model theory |\n| Gödel incompleteness | Response to Russell/Hilbert's logicist program |\n| Computability as epistemology | Turing's machines as models of effective procedure |\n| Hard problem of consciousness | Chalmers — directly engaged in AI consciousness debates |"
    },
