      "text": "The analytic tradition (File 08) is the most directly relevant. Frege invented quantifier logic; Russell tried to reduce mathematics to logic (the project that birthed type theory); Wittgenstein's Tractatus is a formal theory of representation; Quine's critique of analyticity echoes debates about specification and semantics."
