      },
      "text": "| Term | What It Means | Who It's Central To |\n|------|--------------|---------------------|\n| **A priori / a posteriori** | Known independent of / dependent on experience | Kant |\n| **Analytic / synthetic** | True by meaning alone / true by fact about world | Kant; contested by Quine |\n| **Substance** | What exists independently; substrate of properties | Aristotle, Descartes, Spinoza |\n| **Form (eidos)** | Abstract essence; what makes a thing what it is | Plato, Aristotle |\n| **Dialectic** | Reasoning through contradiction to higher synthesis | Plato (dialogue), Hegel |\n| **Categorical imperative** | Act only on maxims you could will to be universal law | Kant |\n| **Will to power** | Not domination but self-overcoming, creative drive | Nietzsche |\n| **Intentionality** | Consciousness is always directed at / about something | Husserl, Brentano |\n| **Being-in-the-world** | Existence is embedded, not a detached observation | Heidegger |\n| **Language games** | Meaning is use in a practice, not reference to objects | Wittgenstein (PI) |\n| **Veil of ignorance** | Design justice principles without knowing your social position | Rawls |\n| **Sense / reference** | Two aspects of meaning: descriptive content vs. what is named | Frege |"
    }
